Summary: Identify the distribution of the data, with quality-control too
 ls and ready-to-run Process Capability syntax
Description: Fits up to 17 distributions by maximum likelihood and repor
 ts goodness of fit (Anderson-Darling, likelihood-ratio tests, AIC, Akai
 ke weights, BIC), parameter estimates, percentiles, capability by distr
 ibution, normalizing transformations, data checks and a recommendation 
 with STATS PROCESS CAPABILITY syntax. Quality-control tools: physical b
 ounds, tolerance intervals, recommendation stability (bootstrap), outli
 er sensitivity, distribution-based control limits, k-sample pooling tes
 t, and saved probabilities and normal scores. Honours Split File and we
 ights. Menu: Analyze > Quality Control > Distribution Identification.
